# QAFlow invariants

`docs/SOP.md` is the source of truth. If code and the SOP disagree, the SOP wins. If the SOP is silent, make the behaviour configurable and add the question to `docs/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md` instead of guessing.

1. AI output is a draft until a human acts. Nothing the model produces is auto-approved.
2. Test cases reach GrokBot only after every item has an explicit human decision and the set is approved.
3. Master test cases are never overwritten or hard-deleted. Changes create a new version, or the case is retired.
4. GrokBot results stay "AI result" until the tester confirms or overrides each one.
5. Only the tester role can give final QA approval.
6. All state changes go through `services/workflow.py` and the audit log.
7. Odoo field names and stage ids are configurable. Never hardcode them.
8. Routers stay thin. Business logic lives in `services/`. Every endpoint has a Pydantic schema and a test.
